1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,000
Jordan’s transfer is about more than changing a user record.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:08,300
Before the move, his application context is the franchise property.

3
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:14,000
A read-only Graph call shows his current workforce account, Harbor View membership and Harborline app assignments.

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:18,700
The managed-property context opens, and the available work changes with it.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,400
We test the old property next. Bayside is refused, so its roster and rooms stay out of reach.

6
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:29,000
Back at Harbor View, Jordan can open the arrival list.

7
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:33,500
He opens Maya’s reservation and sees only matching ready rooms.

8
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,200
Room six oh eight is selected before the app commits the task.

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:43,500
The final screen is the business proof. Maya is in house, and the assignment is visible.
